used_as_mask = true`\n- `mask_width_km = 512.0` (already at 512 km)\n- `clouds_coverage = 0.45` (needs to change to 0.874 per task_config)\n- `atmospheric_density = 1.0` (needs to change to ~0.617977)\n- `cloud_ambient_color = Color(0.8, 0.8, 0.8, 1)` (needs pure white)\n- `cloud_ambient_tint = Color(0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1)` (needs Color(0.131626, 0.201524, 0.241773, 1))\n- `atmosphere_color = Color(0.55, 0.55, 0.55, 1)` (needs Color(0.696127, 0.832325, 0.989334, 1))\n- Has pre-baked light data with a directional light direction/color and a point light position/color\n\n---\n\n## 7. Content of `addons/SunshineClouds2/SunshineCloudsDriver.gd`\n\nThe full file is 272 lines. Key structure:\n\n```gdscript\n@tool\n@icon(\"res://addons/SunshineClouds2/CloudsDriverIcon.svg\")\nextends Node\nclass_name SunshineCloudsDriverGD\n```\n\n**Exported Properties:**\n- `update_continuously: bool` -- toggles continuous updates; setter calls `retrieve_texture_data()`\n- `generate_action` -- tool button that calls `build_new_clouds()`\n- `clouds_resource: SunshineCloudsGD` -- the compositor effect resource\n- `ambience_sample_environment: Environment` -- optional WorldEnvironment reference for fog\n- `use_enviornment_ambience_for_fog: bool`\n- `tracked_directional_lights: Array[DirectionalLight3D]` -- array of lights to track\n- `tracked_directional_light_shadow_steps: Array[int]` -- shadow step counts per light\n- `tracked_point_lights: Array[OmniLight3D]`\n- `tracked_point_effectors: Array[SunshineCloudsEffector]`\n- `directional_light_power_multiplier: float = 1.0`\n- `point_light_power_multiplier: float = 1.0`\n- `origin_offset: Vector3`, `wind_direction: Vector3`\n- Wind speed exports for each noise layer\n\n**Key Methods:**\n- `_process(delta)`: Animates cloud positions, writes all data into `clouds_resource`, checks if lights/effectors changed and re-registers if so\n- `build_new_clouds()`: Creates a new `SunshineCloudsGD` resource, saves it, adds to the compositor, enables update_continuously\n- `recursively_find_env(thisNode)`: Recursively searches node tree for a `WorldEnvironment`\n- `retrieve_texture_data()`: Reads light transforms/colors, populates `directional_lights_data`, `point_lights_data`, `point_effector_data` on the clouds resource\n- `wrap_vector()`, `direction_light_data_changed()`, `point_light_data_changed()`, `point_effector_data_changed()`: Helper utilities\n\n**Important:** The `retrieve_texture_data()` method computes directional light data as `Vector4(look_dir.x, look_dir.y, look_dir.z, shadowSteps)` for the direction and `Vector4(color.r, color.g, color.b, energy)` for the color. Point lights use `Vector4(pos.x, pos.y, pos.z, range)` and `Vector4(color.r, color.g, color.b, energy)`.\n\n---\n\n## 8. WorldEnvironment Analysis\n\nThe **WorldEnvironment** node in `main.tscn` (line 28-30):\n\n```\n[name node=\"WorldEnvironment\" type=\"WorldEnvironment\" parent=\".\"]\nenvironment = SubResource(\"3_env\")\ncompositor = SubResource(\"4_comp\")\n```\n\nWhere `SubResource(\"3_env\")` defines:\n- `background_mode = 2` (Sky)\n- `sky = SubResource(\"2_sky\")` which uses `ProceduralSkyMaterial`\n- `glow_enabled = true`\n- `glow_normalized = true`\n\nAnd `SubResource(\"4_comp\")` defines:\n- `compositor_effects = Array[CompositorEffect]([])` -- **empty array**, meaning the clouds effect is NOT registered in the compositor\n\n**This is a critical finding:** The compositor effects list is empty. For the clouds to render, it needs to contain a reference to the `tutorial_clouds_settings.tres` resource, like:\n```\ncompositor_effects = Array[CompositorEffect]([ExtResource(\"1_clouds\")])\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. DirectionalLight3D and OmniLight3D Nodes\n\n### DirectionalLight3D\n\n```\n[node name=\"DirectionalLight3D\" type=\"DirectionalLight3D\" parent=\".\"]\ntransform = Transform3D(-0.866025, -0.353553, 0.353553, 0, 0.707107, 0.707107, -0.5, 0.612372, -0.612372, -30, 40, -30)\nshadow_enabled = true\n```\n\n- Position: `(-30, 40, -30)`\n- Rotation basis decomposed:\n  - Basis X: `(-0.866025, -0.353553, 0.353553)` -- the negative-Z (forward) direction points roughly at `(0.412799, 0.564261, -0.714988)` which matches the baked directional light data in the `.tres`\n- Shadow: enabled (no explicit shadow step count -- the default is whatever Godot sets)\n\n### OmniLight3D\n\n```\n[node name=\"OmniLight3D\" type=\"OmniLight3D\" parent=\".\"]\ntransform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 25, 10, -45)\nlight_color = Color(1, 0.8, 0.64, 1)\nlight_energy = 12.0\nomni_range = 20000.0\n```\n\n- Position: `(25, 10, -45)` -- identity rotation\n- Color: Orange/warm `(1, 0.8, 0.64)`\n- Energy: `12.0`\n- Range: `20000.0`\n\n---\n\n## 10. Camera3D Configuration\n\n```\n[node name=\"Camera3D\" type=\"Camera3D\" parent=\".\"]\ntransform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 0.965926, 0.258819, 0, -0.258819, 0.965926, 0, 8000, 12000)\nfar = 40000.0\n```\n\n- Position: `(0, 8000, 12000)` -- 8000 units above origin, 12000 units back on Z\n- Rotation: Identity X axis; Y/Z axes tilted (approximately a 15-degree downward pitch, `atan2(0.258819, 0.965926) = 15 degrees`)\n- Far clip plane: `40000.0` (according to `task_config.json`, this needs to be extended to `400000.0`)\n\n---\n\n## 11. Task Config (`task_config.json`)\n\nFor reference, the task_config contains instructions to:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"instruction\": \"Under Main, add a SunshineCloudsDriver node that uses addons/SunshineClouds2/SunshineCloudsDriver.gd, enable Update Continuously, and assign res://assets/clouds/tutorial_clouds_settings.tres to its clouds_resource while reusing the WorldEnvironment environment as ambience_sample_environment. Register the existing DirectionalLight3D and OmniLight3D inside tracked_directional_lights and tracked_point_lights (with a single shadow step entry set to 32) so the clouds use those lights, keep the OmniLight range at 20000, and extend Camera3D's far clip plane to 400000. Wire the same clouds resource into the WorldEnvironment's compositor effect list so the effect renders, and edit assets/clouds/tutorial_clouds_settings.tres to match the reference settings: cloud coverage 0.874, atmospheric density 0.617977, cloud ambient color pure white, ambient tint Color(0.131626, 0.201524, 0.241773, 1), atmosphere color Color(0.696127, 0.832325, 0.989334, 1), and a 512 km mask width so the painted area covers the entire level.\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 12. Example Scene for Reference (`ExampleScene.tscn`)\n\nThis is a working example within the plugin showing the correct structure:\n\n```\nExampleScene (Node3D)\n├── WorldEnvironment (with compositor_effects = [clouds_resource])\n├── DirectionalLight3D\n├── MeshInstance3D (6 cylinder meshes)\n├── PlaneMesh\n├── CapsuleMesh\n├── Label3D\n├── OmniLight3D\n├── SunshineCloudsEffector (Node3D with SunshineCloudEffector.gd)\n├── SunshineCloudsDriverGD (Node with SunshineCloudsDriver.gd)\n│   - update_continuously = true\n│   - clouds_resource = ExtResource(\"1_nv18y\")\n│   - ambience_sample_environment = SubResource(\"Environment_ftegy\")\n│   - tracked_directional_lights = [NodePath(\"../DirectionalLight3D\")]\n│   - tracked_directional_light_shadow_steps = Array[int]([32])\n│   - tracked_point_lights = [NodePath(\"../OmniLight3D\")]\n│   - tracked_point_effectors = [NodePath(\"../SunshineCloudsEffector\")]\n│   - all wind speeds = 0.0\n└── Camera3D (far = 400000.0)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Key Differences Between Current `main.tscn` and What It Needs\n\n| Aspect | Current `main.tscn` | Target (per task_config & ExampleScene) |\n|---|---|---|\n| SunshineCloudsDriverGD node | **Missing** | Add under Main |\n| Clouds resource assignment | N/A | Set to `tutorial_clouds_settings.tres` |\n| ambience_sample_environment | N/A | Point to WorldEnvironment's environment |\n| update_continuously | N/A | true |\n| tracked_directional_lights | N/A | [DirectionalLight3D] |\n| tracked_point_lights | N/A | [OmniLight3D] |\n| tracked_directional_light_shadow_steps | N/A | [32] |\n| Compositor effects list | **Empty** `[]` | Must contain `tutorial_clouds_settings.tres` |\n| Camera3D far clip | `40000.0` | `400000.0` |\n| clouds_coverage | `0.45` | `0.874` |\n| atmospheric_density | `1.0` | `0.617977` |\n| cloud_ambient_color | `Color(0.8, 0.8, 0.8, 1)` | `Color(1, 1, 1, 1)` (pure white) |\n| cloud_ambient_tint | `Color(0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1)` | `Color(0.131626, 0.201524, 0.241773, 1)` |\n| atmosphere_color | `Color(0.55, 0.55, 0.55, 1)` | `Color(0.696127, 0.832325, 0.989334, 1)` |\n| mask_width_km | `512.0` | Already correct |\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f234b347affeUtvGcIfhXnl5SU","sessionId":"ses_f234af173ffe4MpGN6iHFIh4H3","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore project structure","time":{"start":1790409248399,"end":1790409417350}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_1e08962d-dbf5-4bff-be53-ae69ebf068e0"}},"id":"prt_0dcb50e85001aPwuj4QjHw3uyZ","sessionID":"ses_f234b347affeUtvGcIfhXnl5SU","messageID":"msg_0dcb4cd44001IZh3EwJ3qKtVtG"}}
